Article 17 A letter of entrustment for mutual entrustment of taking of evidence between the two sides shall state:
(1) the name of the entrusting court;
(2) the names, addresses and all other circumstances helpful to identify the parties and their litigation agents;
(3) the reasons for entrusting the taking of evidence and the specific matters for which evidence is entrusted to be taken;
(4) the names, addresses and all other circumstances helpful to identify the persons to be investigated, and the questions to be put to them;
(5) the special manner required for taking the evidence;
(6) all other circumstances helpful for the execution of the entrustment.
